cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "snndsl: a domain-specific language and compiler for spiking neural networks"
abstract: >-
  A compiler that takes one description of a spiking neural network and emits
  both PyTorch training code and NIR for neuromorphic hardware, together with
  the tooling to check whether the two agree numerically and whether third-party
  frontends can actually read the result.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/lishangli/snndsl"
url: "https://github.com/lishangli/snndsl"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2025-10-29"
keywords:
  - spiking neural networks
  - neuromorphic computing
  - compiler
  - domain-specific language
  - NIR
  - PyTorch
authors:
  - name: "snndsl contributors"
